{
  "abstract": "We study sub-quadruple regular extensions of two-sided rational Diophantine quintuples in $(r, \\lambda, S_{ab})$, proving the fifth elements are linear in $S_{ab}$ and cut out the Branch 1 sextuple surface $\\mathcal{E}_{\\text{Br1}}$ and twin-fifth surfaces $\\mathcal{E}_{F_1}, \\mathcal{E}_{F_3}$. Factoring $R_4$ on regular fifths defines $\\mathcal{S}_{4, 2}$, collapsing on Branch 1 to a smooth genus-three curve $\\mathcal{H}$ of relation type $(5, 2)$ with unramified $d = 1$ descent and a new rational almost septuple $\\mathcal{S}_7^{(20/21)}$. In global $(r, \\mu, z)$ coordinates, we construct explicit sextuple families, moving-parameter quintuples on $\\mathcal{E}_B$ (with a $2$-adic period-$6$ lock eliminating $Q_4(k) \\equiv -2$), and the universal triple-square section $L_1 = 0$ of $R_5 = \\frac{L_1 L_2 Q_4}{H K^4}$ with rank-$2$ sublattice $\\Lambda(r) \\subset E(r^2)(\\mathbb{Q}(r))$ and rank-$0$ $E_{16}$ closure at $v = -1/5$. On the $3$-torsion inflection surface $\\mathcal{S}_{\\text{3-tors}}$, we establish the Orbit Cubic and Master Syzygies unifying Family IV, DKMS [7], and $\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{triad}}$ (with rank-$0$ $E_{15}$ spoke closure), alongside Mixed-$R_4$ syzygies, $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-2})$ norm $2$-descent closing $H = 1/3$, and Branch B ($20/21$ almost septuple over $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{-14})$). Finally, we prove that enforcing one $R_5$ relation on the four-$R_4$ closure automatically pays $19/21$ conditions ($[1+d_- d_+]=[F_2]=[F_1]=[1]$), construct a rational $\\mathbb{Q}(m)$ family in Source 1 [20] and $23/28$ octuples, close Orbit-I Source 1 by calculator-free Schaefer-Stoll $2$-descent and prime-$5$ Chabauty, and factor the Source 2 exchange quotient in $(q, t)$ (with $D_+^2 D_-^2 = \\square$ and $D_\\pm^2 > 0$ on the real-admissible contact candidate locus, leaving global candidate points open). No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Version 15 incorporating new structural theorems and calculator-free certificates across the Four-R4 closure, the One-R5 locus, the (r, u, v, theta) and (r, u_1, u_2) charts, the Orbit-I Source-1 Jacobian 2-Selmer and Chabauty verification, and the Post 69 exchange-quotient (q, t) factorization and contact-to-source map, all verified symbolically in verify_paper.py (exp9-exp43), verify_jac_selmer.py, and THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md (Theorem 21) in supplement.zip: (1) Four-R4 Opposite-Edge Laws, Double Difference-of-Squares, 4-Factor R_5 Identity, and Automatic 19/21 Payment (Theorems 4(1) & 21(1,2), exp42, exp43, verify_paper.py): On the four-R4 closure (abcd, abce, adfg, befg over P_pair(X) = X^2 - S_{fg} X + w_{fg}^2 - 1 = 0), proved the opposite-edge product identities (1+aX)(1+d_- X) = (w_{fg} - uX)^2 and (1+bX)(1+d_+ X) = (w_{fg} - vX)^2, the Double Difference-of-Squares theorem ab*F_1 = (av - bu)^2 - (a-b)^2 and ab*F_2 = (r^2 - uv)^2 - (u-v)^2 (with Delta_{fg} = F_1*F_2), the 4-factor difference-of-squares identity for R_5(a,b,d_-,d_+,X) on P_pair(X) = 0, and the double binary quadratic discriminant theorem proving [1+d_- d_+] = [F_2] = [F_1] = [1] in Q^x / (Q^x)^2, establishing that enforcing a single terminal R_5 relation on a two-sided quintuple automatically pays Delta_{fg}, 1+d_- d_+, and all eight spokes, elevating the locus to a 19/21 configuration with only cf and cg open; (2) Universal (r, u, v, theta) Conic Chart and (r, u_1, u_2) Conics C_0 and C_mp (Theorems 4(1) & 21(3,5), exp43, verify_paper.py): Parameterized two-sided quintuples on the non-degenerate open locus by (r, u, v, theta) on the conic theta^2 = ((2r^2-1)^2 - u^2)((2r^2-1)^2 - v^2)/(r^2-1) + 4*r^2*u^2*v^2; on the (r, u_1, u_2) threefold, proved that along C_0 : 5r^2 - u_1^2 - 1 = 0, M_{2,mp} = (u_2 - u_1 + 2r)L_mp splits linearly and odd powers of u_1 vanish identically from F_1 = M_{1,-}*M_{1,+}, collapsing M_{1,-}*M_{1,+}/(4r^2) to C_Pyth^2 - B_Pyth^2, while along C_mp : 5r^2 - 5u_1^2 mp 8u_1 - 5 = 0, 4*A_{2,mp}*M_{2,pm} - L_{dbl,mp}^2 = pm 8*A_{2,mp}(u_2 - u_1 + 2r)(r^2 + 2r*u_1 - u_1*u_2 - 1); (3) Complete Calculator-Free Schaefer-Stoll 2-Selmer and Prime-5 Chabauty Exclusion of Orbit-I Source 1 (Theorems 7(6) & 21(3), exp43, verify_jac_selmer.py): On C : y^2 = 228x^6 + 595x^5 + 1457x^4 + 1904x^3 + 3296x^2 + 1024x + 2304 (x = -1/H), proved J(Q)_tors = (Z/2Z)^2 via gcd(#J(F_5), #J(F_13)) = gcd(12, 128) = 4, proved rank J(Q) = 1 via Schaefer-Stoll (H - T) 2-descent [24] over Q(sqrt(-7)) and Q(sqrt(-2)) at S = {2, 3, 7, 11} with ker(delta) = <[inf_- - inf_+]> ~= Z/2Z and the exact 14x21 F_2 pivot matrix giving dim Sel_quot^(2) = 2 => dim J(Q)/2J(Q) <= 3 => rank J(Q) = 1, and for P_pm = (0, pm 48) in C(Q) reducing to p_0, p_1 = (0, pm 2) in C(F_5), proved 3[P_+ - P_-] in J_1(Q_5) with mod-25 Coleman integrals I_0 = I_1 = 20 [25] and normalized differential omega_tilde_ann = 4(1-x)dx/(2y) (mod 5) having unit leading coefficient 4 on both disks; (4) Post 69 Exchange-Quotient (q, t) Source Factorization and Contact-to-Source Map (Theorems 7(6) & 21(5), exp43): On Paper 75's second paired source [20], proved -(16(q-1)^3 T^2 - q) = L_1(q, t)*L_2(q, t)/t^2 with original chart c^2 = q*L_2/(16(q-1)^4 L_1), D^2 = q(8q-9)/(16(q-1)^4 L_1) and exchange-conjugate chart G^2 = K^2/c^2 = q(4q-5)^2 L_1/L_2, D_conj^2 = t^2(8q-9)/L_2; on the contact candidate curve B^2 = -(7q+9)(45q^2-25q-36), H^2 = q^4+64q^3+1054q^2-1440q+81, substituted F and u, z to obtain the exact branch lifts D_pm^2 = W_pm(q)/(8(q-1)^2 B^2) whose product D_+^2 * D_-^2 = (e(2q^2+63q-81)/(4(q-1)^2 B))^2 is identically a rational square, proved local 3-adic unit obstruction v_3(H^2) = 1 (3 not dividing e), H^2 < 0 on (q_{H, 1}, q_{H, 2}) (q_{H, 1} in (0, 1/17), q_{H, 2} in (6/5, 1213/1000)), and real positivity D_pm^2 > 0 throughout (0, q_{H, 1}] union [q_{H, 2}, q_{B, +}] (q_{B, +} in (1213/1000, 5/4)), leaving global candidate points open.",
